## TECHNOLOGY STACK INTEGRATION

### Microsoft Semantic Kernel (SK) Agent Framework v1.57+
- **ChatCompletionAgent**: Full function calling support with auto-mode
- **Multi-Agent Orchestration**: Sequential, Concurrent, GroupChat, Handoff, Magentic patterns
- **AgentThreads**: Conversation state management and context preservation
- **Function Calling**: Automatic skill invocation when LLM determines need

### SK Process Framework
- **Long-Running Workflows**: Stateful processes that can pause and resume
- **Author-Critic Loops**: AI draft followed by review with quality thresholds
- **Refine Loops**: Iterative improvement with termination conditions
- **Process Integration**: Seamless integration with Agent Framework

### Prompty (Declarative Prompt Templates)
- **YAML Format**: External prompt definitions with system instructions and examples
- **Runtime Loading**: Dynamic prompt loading without recompilation
- **Context Variables**: Placeholder system for runtime context injection
- **Version Control**: Independent versioning and testing of prompts

### Microsoft.Extensions.AI
- **Unified Abstractions**: Standardized AI service management
- **Dependency Injection**: Seamless integration with .NET DI container
- **Middleware Support**: OpenTelemetry, caching, and function invocation pipelines
- **Model Agnostic**: Easy switching between OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, and local models

### Ollama (Local LLM Hosting)
- **On-Premises Deployment**: Local model hosting for privacy and cost control
- **IChatClient Integration**: Implemented as SK skill or Extensions.AI client
- **Model Selection**: Dynamic model selection based on task complexity
- **Air-Gapped Support**: Functionality without internet connectivity

### Clean Architecture & Ultra-Generic Design
- **Domain Layer**: Abstract concepts and interfaces
- **Application Layer**: SK Kernel and agent orchestration logic
- **Infrastructure Layer**: Concrete skills and external integrations
- **Configuration Management**: Data-driven configuration for dynamic adjustment

